# Chroma library, modern Earth: SEEKING AND REPAIR MOMENTS (v25 prep, Library, 10-23). Goes to chroma-library/earth_seek.lib.
# Syntax: header of chroma-library/build.py, with the v25 keys state: (moment) and seek: / repair: (option).
# Rule: Emren's v25 decisions, section 4 (decision #4) and section 2; keys: chroma-engine/notes/v25/contracts.md, 4.
# Eighteen life events, per_year 0 everywhere: the Engine sends a seeking moment when a state applies, and a repair
# moment when a tie is strained. Nothing reads this file until the Engine's seek switch is on, so no life changes.
# Nothing here is built or run.
#
# A. Seeking, ten moments, two per state (state: boredom | frustration | anger | content | low_mood). States never come
#    from a colour, and no option here says one does. Seeking moves what draws them; it never grants entry: every option
#    toward a new setting is an attempt (go along, put a name down, turn up), and the works and fails lines show an
#    admission, a cold welcome, or a fit that surprises.
# B. Repair, eight moments about one strained tie each (partner x3, friend x2, parent of a grown child x1, sibling x1,
#    colleague x1). No cast_want:; life: names the area. Separate is at most two options in a moment and never the
#    default; the works lines show what staying makes. Time, money, chores, plans, hurt words and distance only.
#
# Balance layout: five one-colour options and one full cross cycle per moment, the cycles alternating through the
# file (s1 W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W, s2 W>B U>R B>G R>W G>U): odd moments s1, even moments s2, nine of each.
#
# Plan (option order W U B R G, then the cycle's five crosses in the order above):
#
#   seeking                 cycle  W        U        B        R        G        | crosses
#   1 same day (boredom)    s1     persist  revise   deepen   help     own_int  | method   negot    persist  revise   deepen
#   2 pastime (boredom)     s2     own_int  keep     withdr   method   negot    | deepen   help     own_int  keep     withdr
#   3 piece (frustration)   s1     negot    persist  revise   deepen   help     | withdr   method   negot    persist  revise
#   4 door (frustration)    s2     withdr   method   negot    persist  revise   | own_int  keep     withdr   method   negot
#   5 told (anger)          s1     method   negot    persist  revise   deepen   | keep     withdr   method   negot    persist
#   6 mark (anger)          s2     keep     withdr   method   negot    persist  | help     own_int  keep     withdr   method
#   7 season (content)      s1     deepen   help     own_int  keep     withdr   | persist  revise   deepen   help     own_int
#   8 offer (content)       s2     revise   deepen   help     own_int  keep     | negot    persist  revise   deepen   help
#   9 flat weeks (low_mood) s1     help     own_int  keep     withdr   method   | revise   deepen   help     own_int  keep
#  10 ended (low_mood)      s2     deepen   help     own_int  keep     withdr   | persist  revise   deepen   help     own_int
#
#   repair                  cycle  W        U        B        R        G        | crosses
#  11 evenings (partner)    s1     talk     separ    bound    routine  reneg    | shared   talk     repair   bound    routine
#  12 money (partner)       s2     repair   bound    routine  reneg    shared   | separ    repair   bound    routine  talk
#  13 plan (partner)        s1     bound    routine  reneg    shared   separ    | repair   talk     routine  reneg    shared
#  14 cancels (friend)      s2     routine  reneg    shared   talk     repair   | bound    routine  separ    shared   talk
#  15 joke (friend)         s1     reneg    shared   talk     separ    bound    | routine  reneg    shared   talk     repair
#  16 calls (parent)        s2     shared   talk     separ    bound    routine  | reneg    shared   talk     repair   separ
#  17 always (sibling)      s1     separ    repair   bound    routine  reneg    | shared   talk     repair   bound    routine
#  18 carried (colleague)   s2     repair   bound    routine  reneg    shared   | talk     separ    talk     separ    reneg
#
# Colour by tag over the whole file, counted by the option's leading colour (single + cross led = total):
#
#   seek          W          U          B          R          G
#   deepen        2+1 = 3    1+1 = 2    1+2 = 3    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2
#   method        1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2
#   help          1+1 = 2    2+1 = 3    1+1 = 2    1+2 = 3    1+1 = 2
#   negotiate     1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2
#   own_interest  1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    2+1 = 3    1+1 = 2    1+2 = 3
#   persist       1+2 = 3    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2
#   keep          1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    2+1 = 3    1+1 = 2
#   revise        1+1 = 2    1+2 = 3    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2
#   withdraw      1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    2+1 = 3
#
#   repair        W          U          B          R          G
#   talk          1+1 = 2    1+3 = 4    1+2 = 3    1+1 = 2    0+2 = 2
#   repair        2+1 = 3    1+1 = 2    0+2 = 2    0+1 = 1    1+1 = 2
#   boundary      1+1 = 2    2+0 = 2    2+1 = 3    1+2 = 3    1+0 = 1
#   routine       1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    2+1 = 3    2+1 = 3    1+2 = 3
#   renegotiate   1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+0 = 1    2+1 = 3    2+1 = 3
#   shared        1+2 = 3    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    2+1 = 3
#   separate      1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2    1+1 = 2
#
# Every seek tag goes to all five colours (2 or 3 each); every repair tag to all five (1 to 4); separate is 2 per
# colour and at most two options in any moment.
#
# Ages: seeking 12-90 (the work moment 16-75, the refusals 14-90, the content offer 14-90); repair: partners 16-90,
# parent of a grown child 18-80, sibling 14-90, colleague 16-75, friends 12-90. Nothing under 12. No bars, no drinking.


# ================================================================ A. SEEKING

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1. boredom, at work (cycle s1)

== the same day, every day
tier: life event
state: boredom
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-75
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: work
horizon: months
roles: colleague, boss, friend, mentor, elder
earth: a job done well for so long that it no longer asks anything of {N}
tribal: the same task at the camp, season after season, done without a thought
magic: the same duty in the guild hall every day, so practised it no longer needs the mind
scene: {N} can do the work with eyes half shut now, and most days that is how it gets done. The hours are fine, the pay is fine, {colleague} is fine, and by noon {N} is counting minutes. Nothing is wrong, and that is the trouble.
scene tribal: {N} has tended the fish traps every day for many seasons, and the hands do it alone now. The talk at the fire is the same talk. {elder} says a task done well is enough; {N} is not sure it is.
scene magic: In the guild hall {N} copies the same wards onto the same doors, and the ink barely needs watching. {mentor} has stopped checking the work. The days are safe, and each one is exactly like the last.
- W | keep the work to its proper standard, and put the spare hours into savings | v: conformity, security | seek: persist | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 85
- U | write down what the job was meant to lead to, and whether it still should | v: self-direction | seek: revise | foot: lesson an old aim can retire | chance: 75
- B | push for the hardest account in the place, the one nobody wants | v: achievement, power | seek: deepen | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- R | ask {friend} for a plan, any plan, for the free evenings this month | v: stimulation, hedonism | seek: help | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 80
- G | put a name down for a plot at the allotments, to walk to after work | v: self-direction, security | seek: own_interest | foot: place prod.land | chance: 70
- W>U | apply for the evening certificate that leads to the next grade, every form done right | v: conformity, achievement | seek: method | foot: place learn.higher | chance: 65
- U>B | show {boss} the figures for a faster method, and ask for the freed hours | v: self-direction, power | seek: negotiate | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 60
- B>R | do the job as it is, fast, and spend the saved energy on the weekends | v: hedonism, security | seek: persist | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 80
- R>G | drop the plan to rise at this firm, and look at work outdoors instead | v: stimulation, universalism | seek: revise | foot: door took a wild risk | chance: 55
- G>W | offer to teach the new starters, and go deeper into the craft by teaching it | v: benevolence, conformity | seek: deepen | foot: person colleague | chance: 80
works: A few weeks on, the days have an edge again, and {N} catches the clock less often.
works: The new thing does not fit the way {N} expected. It fits in another way, and that turns out better.
fails: The door {N} knocks on opens onto polite faces and no seat, and the old days are waiting where they were.
fails: Nothing much changes. The flatness stays, but {N} now knows one more thing it is not about.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2. boredom, at home and in a pastime (cycle s2)

== the pastime gone flat
tier: life event
state: boredom
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: play, home
horizon: months
roles: friend, sibling
earth: the weekend pastime that used to fill the hours, and now fills nothing
tribal: the evening game by the fire that used to be the best part of the day
magic: the little charms {N} used to spend whole evenings on, now left half-made
scene: For years the weekends belonged to one pastime: the drawing, the bike rides, the long games with {friend}. Lately {N} sets it out and puts it away again an hour later without having started. The free hours are there, and they feel empty.
scene tribal: The stone-throwing game by the fire used to be the best part of {Ns} day. Now {N} sits at the edge and watches {friend} play, and the evenings drag. Nobody has noticed but {N}.
scene magic: {N} used to spend whole evenings coaxing small charms out of string and wax. The half-made ones pile up on the sill now, and {friend} asks why the window has stopped glowing.
- W | start a proper weekly club for the pastime, with a time and a place kept | v: conformity, benevolence | seek: own_interest | foot: place gather.hall | chance: 60
- U | keep a set hour for the pastime each week, bored or not, and note what changes | v: self-direction, security | seek: keep | foot: lesson interest can come back slowly | chance: 80
- B | put the whole thing away for a season, and spend the hours earning | v: achievement, security | seek: withdraw | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 85
- R | try the same pastime a new way: outdoors, at dawn, somewhere never tried | v: stimulation | seek: method | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 75
- G | offer to share it with {sibling} for a while, taking turns to choose what to do | v: benevolence, tradition | seek: negotiate | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 75
- W>B | enter the open contest for it, and train to a real standard | v: achievement, conformity | seek: deepen | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- U>R | ask the oldest hand at the club what made it exciting for them, and try that | v: self-direction, stimulation | seek: help | foot: person mentor | chance: 70
- B>G | turn up at the open day of the walking club, just to see who is there | v: achievement, benevolence | seek: own_interest | foot: place gather.games | chance: 65
- R>W | keep the standing game with {friend} every week, even on the flat days | v: benevolence, conformity | seek: keep | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 80
- G>U | step back from all of it, and let the free hours stay free for a while | v: security, self-direction | seek: withdraw | foot: lesson empty hours can rest | chance: 85
works: {N} turns up half expecting nothing, and an hour passes without a glance at the clock.
works: It is not the old pleasure back. It is a new one, smaller and sharper, and {N} keeps it.
fails: The welcome is polite and thin, and {N} walks home early to the same empty evening.
fails: The flatness lasts the season. Something is changing, and {N} cannot yet see into what.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3. frustration, help near (cycle s1)

== the piece that breaks at the same place
tier: life event
state: frustration
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: learning, play
horizon: months
roles: mentor, friend, grandparent, neighbour, elder
earth: months of work on one skill, and it still breaks at the same place every time
tribal: the bow {N} has shaped all season, which still splits at the same knot
magic: a spell practised for months, which still fizzles at the same word
scene: For months {N} has worked at one thing, a tune on the old piano, a joint in the wood, a stubborn page of figures, and it still breaks at the same place. {mentor} has watched twice and plainly would help if asked. Every evening the same mistake arrives on time.
scene tribal: All season {N} has shaped bows from the same kind of wood, and every one splits at the knot. {elder}, who has made bows for longer than anyone, sits three fires away. {N} has not asked.
scene magic: {N} has practised the lighting spell for months, and it fizzles at the same word every time. {mentor} keeps an open door in the tower for anyone stuck, and {N} has walked past it twice this week.
- W | ask for a proper extra hour in the practice room, and agree to keep it tidy | v: conformity, achievement | seek: negotiate | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 75
- U | go back to it every evening, slowly, until the break shows its cause | v: self-direction, achievement | seek: persist | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 55
- B | trade the hard piece for one that can win something sooner | v: achievement, power | seek: revise | foot: lesson pick the battle worth winning | chance: 80
- R | throw every hour at it for one wild week, morning and night | v: stimulation, achievement | seek: deepen | foot: means health-.03 | chance: 60
- G | ask {mentor} to sit alongside and watch the hands, just once | v: benevolence, tradition | seek: help | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 85
- W>U | set it aside until next term, as the teacher's plan says | v: conformity, security | seek: withdraw | foot: lesson rest is part of practice | chance: 85
- U>B | film the attempts, find the exact moment it fails, and drill only that | v: self-direction, achievement | seek: method | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 70
- B>R | strike a deal at home: all the chores done, and the practice room free all weekend | v: power, stimulation | seek: negotiate | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 70
- R>G | play it badly and loudly in the yard until it is fun again | v: stimulation, hedonism | seek: persist | foot: person neighbour | chance: 75
- G>W | promise {grandparent} a plain version by summer, not a perfect one | v: benevolence, tradition | seek: revise | foot: door kept your word | chance: 80
works: The break gives way one evening, quietly, and {N} gets through the whole thing twice, to be sure it was not luck.
works: It is still not right, but it breaks later now, and {N} can see the end from here.
fails: The same place, the same break. {N} is tired of the sound of it.
fails: A new mistake joins the old one, and the week ends further back than it began.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 4. frustration, no help near (cycle s2)

== the door that keeps saying no
tier: life event
state: frustration
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 14-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: work, learning
horizon: months
roles: friend, parent
earth: the third refusal from the place {N} has worked toward, and nobody nearby who ever got in
tribal: the hunters' band that turns {N} away again, and no kin who ever ran with it
magic: the academy's third refusal, and not one person in the village who has passed its gate
scene: The third letter says no, as kindly as the first two: no place this year. {N} has done everything the guidance asked, and nobody in the family or the street has ever got through this door to say what is missing. {friend} means well and knows nothing about it.
scene tribal: For the third season the hunters' band has turned {N} away at the gathering. None of {Ns} kin ever ran with them, so nobody can say what the band wants. {friend} shrugs and offers to go fishing instead.
scene magic: The academy's third refusal comes sealed in wax, with no reason given. Nobody in {Ns} village has ever passed its gate, and {friend} has never even seen it.
- W | stop applying for now, and do the waiting job properly | v: conformity, security | seek: withdraw | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 85
- U | study the lists of past entrants, and work out what the ones admitted had in common | v: self-direction, achievement | seek: method | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | write to the person in charge directly, and ask what it would take | v: power, achievement | seek: negotiate | foot: lesson ask the gate itself | chance: 55
- R | apply again straight away, the same way, with everything poured into it | v: stimulation, achievement | seek: persist | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- G | turn the aim toward the nearer course that people from around here get into | v: security, tradition | seek: revise | foot: place learn.higher | chance: 75
- W>B | start a small study group of the others who were turned down, and set its pace | v: conformity, power | seek: own_interest | foot: place gather.talk | chance: 60
- U>R | hold to the promise made at the start: one more honest try, then think again | v: self-direction, stimulation | seek: keep | foot: door kept your word | chance: 80
- B>G | take the year at home, and let the whole thing cool | v: security, benevolence | seek: withdraw | foot: mark stayed home | chance: 85
- R>W | turn up in person on the open day, and ask to be seen | v: stimulation, conformity | seek: method | foot: person mentor | chance: 55
- G>U | ask whether a part-time place or a later start could be arranged | v: benevolence, self-direction | seek: negotiate | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 60
works: A different answer comes at last: a place, a yes with conditions, or someone who explains what the letters never did.
works: The no stands, but {N} can see the gap now, and a way across it that does not need this door.
fails: Another polite no, and still nobody to ask why.
fails: The new way in is open, but the welcome is cool, and {N} sits at the back wondering if it was worth it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 5. anger, at a person (cycle s1)

== the private thing told to everyone
tier: life event
state: anger
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: friends
horizon: week
roles: friend
earth: something {N} said in confidence, now going round everyone
tribal: a thing told to {friend} at the stream, now repeated around every fire
magic: a secret shared with {friend}, now whispered through the whole guild
scene: Something {N} told {friend} in confidence is going round everyone, and it came back today in someone else's mouth. {friend} has not said sorry, or even mentioned it. The anger sits in {Ns} chest all afternoon and will not go down.
scene tribal: A thing {N} told {friend} at the stream is being repeated around every fire tonight. {friend} laughs with the others as if it were nothing. {N} cannot eat.
scene magic: A secret {N} trusted to {friend} is being whispered through the guild's halls. {friend} passes {N} on the stair without a word. The anger hums like a badly bound ward.
- W | write down calmly exactly what was broken, and set a time to go through it | v: conformity, universalism | seek: method | foot: lesson calm words carry further | chance: 75
- U | tell {friend} the new terms plainly: no more confidences until trust is rebuilt | v: self-direction, security | seek: negotiate | foot: means ties-.03 | chance: 75
- B | carry on as before in public, and keep score in private | v: power, security | seek: persist | foot: door kept it hidden | chance: 85
- R | decide {friend} is not the friend it seemed, and expect less from now on | v: self-direction, stimulation | seek: revise | foot: person friend lost | chance: 70
- G | spend more time with {friend}, not less, until the reason comes out | v: benevolence | seek: deepen | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 60
- W>U | keep the old promise between them, and repeat nothing about {friend} to anyone | v: tradition, self-direction | seek: keep | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 80
- U>B | step back from the shared group for a few weeks, and watch who asks why | v: self-direction, power | seek: withdraw | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 80
- B>R | say exactly what was broken, sharply, in front of the people who heard the story | v: power, stimulation | seek: method | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- R>G | tell {friend} how much it hurt, loudly and honestly, and ask for a new start | v: stimulation, benevolence | seek: negotiate | foot: lesson honest anger can mend | chance: 65
- G>W | let it pass, as old friends do, and keep turning up | v: tradition, benevolence | seek: persist | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 85
works: The anger runs its course, and what is left can be talked about. Something between them is clearer, if not the same.
works: {friend} understands at last what was broken, and the next secret {N} chooses to tell is kept.
fails: Nothing is settled. The story keeps going round, and {N} keeps hearing it.
fails: It goes badly: words are said that make it worse, and both of them walk away hot in the face.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 6. anger, at a rule or a body (cycle s2)

== the mark that should not stand
tier: life event
state: anger
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: work, learning
horizon: months
roles: mentor, friend, elder
earth: a mark on {Ns} record for something {N} did not do, and a rule that says it stands
tribal: blame laid on {N} at the council fire for a lost net, and the custom that blame once spoken stays
magic: a demerit in the guild's book for a broken ward {N} never touched
scene: The people who run things have put a mark on {Ns} record for something {N} did not do, and the rule says a mark, once entered, stands. The one who did it is known and untouched. {N} reads the letter three times and is angrier each time.
scene tribal: At the council fire the loss of the big net was laid on {N}, though {N} was upriver that day. Custom says blame once spoken is not unsaid, and {elder} looks away.
scene magic: The guild's book now shows a demerit beside {Ns} name for a broken ward {N} never touched. The guild's law says entries are never struck out. {friend} heard someone laughing about it on the stair.
- W | keep working by the rules anyway, and let the clean record that follows answer | v: conformity, security | seek: keep | foot: lesson a clean record answers back | chance: 80
- U | stop volunteering for anything there, and do only what is required | v: self-direction, security | seek: withdraw | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 85
- B | find the clause that says when a mark can be struck out, and use it | v: power, achievement | seek: method | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 55
- R | go to the office in person, and argue for a hearing to their faces | v: stimulation, universalism | seek: negotiate | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 50
- G | carry on as before, and trust the people who know {N} to know better | v: tradition, benevolence | seek: persist | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 80
- W>B | find someone respected to speak at the review, and ask them properly | v: conformity, power | seek: help | foot: person go-between | chance: 60
- U>R | start a small newsletter setting out how the rule fails people | v: universalism, self-direction | seek: own_interest | foot: place rule.voice | chance: 60
- B>G | stay on with the team anyway, and make sure everyone hears the truth | v: benevolence, power | seek: keep | foot: person friend | chance: 75
- R>W | walk out of the place for good, and say why in writing | v: stimulation, universalism | seek: withdraw | foot: means freedom+.05 | chance: 70
- G>U | gather the others the rule has caught, and look at the cases together | v: benevolence, universalism | seek: method | foot: place gather.talk | chance: 65
works: The mark is struck out at last, with a dry note and no apology, and {N} keeps the letter anyway.
works: The mark stays, but the rule is looked at again, and the next one caught by it will have an easier time.
fails: The mark stands. The people who run things have moved on, and only {N} is still angry.
fails: It turns sour: the complaint becomes its own mark, and {N} learns how the place treats people who object.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 7. content, keeping a good thing going (cycle s1)

== the good season
tier: life event
state: content
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: joy
life: home, friends
horizon: months
roles: friend, grandparent, neighbour
earth: a stretch of life where the days fit and the people are near
tribal: a fat season at the camp, the stores full and the songs easy
magic: a calm season in the realm, the wards holding and the house warm
scene: Things are good. The days have a shape {N} likes, {friend} is near, and the work or the school asks enough and not too much. {N} notices it one evening on the walk home, and wonders what it takes to keep it.
scene tribal: The stores are full, the hunting has been kind, and the songs at the fire come easily. {N} sits with {friend} and feels it plainly: this is a good season. The old ones say good seasons need tending.
scene magic: The wards hold, the harvest charms took, and the house is warm with people {N} loves. {friend} calls it a lucky year, and {N} wonders whether luck needs looking after.
- W | give more time to what makes it good: the shared meals, the standing plans | v: tradition, conformity | seek: deepen | foot: place gather.house | chance: 85
- U | ask {grandparent} what kept the good years good, and listen to the answer | v: self-direction, tradition | seek: help | foot: lesson good things need tending | chance: 85
- B | start a small trade on the side while the ground is steady | v: achievement, security | seek: own_interest | foot: means money+.04 | chance: 70
- R | keep the weekly evening with {friend} free, whatever else comes up | v: hedonism, benevolence | seek: keep | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 85
- G | step back from the extra things, and let the good days be quiet ones | v: security, tradition | seek: withdraw | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 90
- W>U | carry on exactly as now: the same days, kept with care | v: conformity, security | seek: persist | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 90
- U>B | set one small new aim on top of the good days, and see what it costs | v: achievement, self-direction | seek: revise | foot: lesson aims can grow from rest | chance: 75
- B>R | make more room for the best part: the music, the games, whatever lights the week | v: hedonism, achievement | seek: deepen | foot: place arts.song | chance: 80
- R>G | ask the friends round for a big shared meal, and let them help make it | v: benevolence, hedonism | seek: help | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 85
- G>W | start a small shared garden with the neighbours, to keep the street close | v: universalism, benevolence | seek: own_interest | foot: person neighbour | chance: 70
works: The season lasts longer than {N} dared hope, and some of it simply becomes how life is.
works: A small change keeps the good thing fresh, and {N} learns what keeping something going feels like.
fails: The good season thins out on its own, the way seasons do, and {N} is glad of what it was.
fails: The new thing costs more than it gives, and {N} has to win the old calm back.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 8. content, a new pull anyway (cycle s2)

== the offer on a good day
tier: life event
state: content
