scene: Life is good: the days fit and the people are near. Then {friend} mentions an opening somewhere new, a team, a course, a crew in another town, and says {N} would be good at it. {N} was not looking, and cannot stop thinking about it.
scene tribal: The season at home is good, the stores full and the fire warm. A travelling band passing through invites {N} to walk with them over the mountains to the summer grounds, and {elder} says nothing either way. {N} has not slept well since.
scene magic: Life in the village is settled and kind. Then a letter comes from the far academy: a place, if {N} wants it, from the next moon. {N} reads it on the porch with the sun on the page, and does not know what to feel.
