magic: a season when even the house-lights burn low, and nobody can say why
scene: For weeks now the days have weighed a little more than they should. Nothing in particular is wrong; getting up is slower, and the things that used to help help less. {friend} has noticed and not said anything yet.
scene tribal: The days are short, and for weeks {N} has felt the fire grow smaller and the walk to the water grow longer. Nobody is ill and nothing is lost. {friend} sits beside {N} more often than before.
