scene: Every month {N} and {partner} have the same argument about money, and it goes the same way: one spends, one worries, both say things they regret. This month it started over something small and ended in silence. The account is not empty; the trust around it is thin.
scene tribal: Every moon {N} and {partner} quarrel over the stores: who traded away the good skins, who keeps back too much. This moon it ended in silence by the fire. There is enough to eat, and not enough trust about it.
scene magic: Every moon {N} and {partner} argue over the household purse, word for word the same. This moon {partner} went to sleep in the other room. The purse is not empty; the trust around it is thin.
- W | own up to the spending that was kept quiet, and lay out the real figures | v: conformity, universalism | repair: repair | foot: mark owned up | chance: 70
- U | set a firm line for both: no big purchase without a day's notice to the other | v: self-direction, security | repair: boundary | foot: door kept your word | chance: 75
- B | set a fixed money hour each week, with the figures on the table | v: power, security | repair: routine | foot: lesson numbers calm the room | chance: 75
