scene: {N} finishes the class work in ten minutes and spends the rest of the lesson watching the window. The marks are fine, the teacher is fine, {friend} is fine, and by the second lesson {N} is counting the minutes to the bell. Nothing is hard, and nothing is asking anything either.
scene tribal: {N} learned the names of the stars and the moods of the river two winters ago, and still sits through them every night at the elders' fire. {friend} dozes; {N} draws patterns in the dust with a stick. {grandparent} has noticed, and says nothing yet.
scene magic: At the academy {N} has known the first-year drills by heart since autumn, and still chants them every morning with the rest. The master sets the same small ward again, and {N} finishes it before the candle has settled. Behind the closed doors of the tower, harder work goes on.
